sentences.l:
But he avoided it, Odysseus,
gently bending his head aside, and smiled in his heart
bitterly, so very much so;

But nevertheless these things at least we even endure, looking on,
flocks being slaughtered and wine being drunk
and food;

for so long there was no resentment, that they should stay and hold back,
the suitors, throughout the house, since this was better,
if Odysseus came home and, returning, reached his house;

But of supper, in no way a more graceless other could come to be,
of the kind that soon were going the goddess and the strong man
to set;
